  unit: { count: 123, covers: "The platform axis and each member's instruction set — the eight members and their order, the two platforms a probe can answer for, the five that need reach, the emulator against the device (reach, certificate route and host all different), the prose-punt guard, the copyable-exactly-once discipline and the save control's placement. DEC-33's resolution after its move: the nineteen verdicts asserted literally, the recency table and the precedence rules, with the three sentences that named a step the screen no longer has rewritten. The screen: one axis and no stepper, the probe row's scope, the un-probeable verdicts in their own words, the one-click actions scoped to this machine, both halves of DEC-13's reversal rule, the unarmed and armed off-machine renderings, the address cardinality rule at its three boundaries, the seven verdict readings, the guide's inline and auto-open promises, the way out, the tick's scope, and the single scroller. The review's findings, each pinned: a headline that is still checking never carries an announcement of capture beneath it (the regression test, written before the fix), a verdict that implies an instruction renders both elements, a failure is stated once rather than twice, and a renamed save is confirmed against the name the steps beside it actually use. Notice tone=pending: a spinner in the glyph column, the sentence still mute, the three shipped tones unchanged." }
  integration: { count: 56, covers: "The seam this WU owns — the screen's contract with the machine and the API, neither half observable from a test of the screen alone. Reach is read on entering setup rather than assumed. Arming costs one confirm and a refusal costs nothing: confirm_reach is invoked with the selected address, a false answer makes no POST and leaves the screen unarmed, a true answer arms that address and the screen renders the addresses the response carried. Disarming needs no second dialog. A core that will not answer leaves the screen saying Trawler answers here only. Plus the seams the rebuilt screen inherits: install fetches the PEM and invokes install_ca, set_proxy carries the split address, the save writes the certificate under the name the steps run against, the probes drive both preconditions and are re-read by check again and by window focus, and a tunnel leads the screen and puts its remedy inside the precondition it instructs." }
  e2e: { waived: "The epic owes the e2e and W4 takes it — the spine is rewritten against the platform axis with a coverage map over the 8 assertions the current spec holds. ui/e2e/specs/onboarding.spec.ts is stale at this tip on purpose: editing its assertions here would land a spec asserting a screen nobody designed." }
